  "caption": "Constructed illustration. The hypothetical benefit and refundable tax credit give identical net income, with a $5,000 drop immediately above $30,000 of annual earnings. The continuous benefit taper changes slope at $30,000 and $40,000 without a downward jump. Filled circles mark included endpoints; open circles mark excluded branch limits. For notch terminology, see Kleven and Waseem (2013), Quarterly Journal of Economics 128(2), 669-723: https://doi.org/10.1093/qje/qjt004.",
